					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 1: USING MULTIPLY TO SCALE INPUTS\n\nIn this example we are using a Float In node renamed to Scale that runs from 0 to 100.\nBut the Transform node wants a normalized scale value (0-1).\nSo we multiply by 0.01 to get back to a 0 to 1 range.\n\nWe as code savvy maniacs know what is going on, but for the user a 0-100% range might make more sense."
					}
				},
